Z||000006||AusFiero||07-18-2001||01:03 PM||||I know you guys use dye and such but there is another method. Our dyes here are pretty low quality. <P>To remove armorall use Prepsol (wax and grease remover as used by panel beaters). Do this baout 3 times with new rags each time to be certain. Then about 5 minutes before painting the part wipe it over with a damp (not wet at all) rag with thinners on it. This makes the surface soften and then plain old acrylic paint bites into it as good as any dye. <P>Have to be careful though as it isn't an easy process and is easy to destroy old interior parts.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||1
